# Jötun Grunt: "Put two cards from a single graveyard on the bottom of their owner's library." Bot1's graveyard holds two Lotus
# Petals and Bot2's one, so the only graveyard two cards can come from is Bot1's: at the turn 3 upkeep Bot1 is not asked which
# graveyard (Bot2's has too few to be one), and puts both Petals on the bottom of their library. Bot2's stays.

[Bot1 Deck]
Jötun Grunt
Lotus Petal
Lotus Petal
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Lotus Petal
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Lotus Petal.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Lotus Petal.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Lotus Petal#1.Activate(Color: White)
Bot1.Battlefield.Lotus Petal#1.Activate(Color: White)
Bot1.Hand.Jötun Grunt.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Lotus Petal.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Lotus Petal.Activate(Color: Blue)
[T3 Bot1.Upkeep]
? Stack.Count = 1
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Accept
! Bot1.ChoosePlayer
Bot1.Choose(Lotus Petal; Lotus Petal)
Bot1.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Jötun Grunt.Counters.Age = 1

[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard.Count = 0
Bot2.Graveyard = Lotus Petal
